1
00:00:25,926 --> 00:00:28,160
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,503 --> 00:00:38,336
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,416 --> 00:00:51,450
♪ ♪

4
00:01:09,703 --> 00:01:11,637
♪ ♪

5
00:03:19,966 --> 00:03:21,934
Hi, this is Linda Hansfield.

6
00:03:22,002 --> 00:03:23,969
I can't take your
call right now,

7
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:26,015
but if you leave your name
and number at the beep,

8
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,150
I'll get right back to you.

9
00:03:27,174 --> 00:03:28,174
Thanks.

10
00:03:32,779 --> 00:03:35,380
This is Larry, uh,
at Pronto Printing.

11
00:03:35,449 --> 00:03:37,215
Your business cards are ready.

12
00:03:37,284 --> 00:03:38,716
Say, maybe when you pick 'em up,

13
00:03:38,785 --> 00:03:40,430
we could go for a
drink or something.

14
00:03:40,454 --> 00:03:41,919
What do you say?

15
00:03:43,023 --> 00:03:44,456
Hello, Mrs. Hansfield,

16
00:03:44,524 --> 00:03:46,124
this is Rosemary Barnes.

17
00:03:46,193 --> 00:03:48,426
That matter we
talked about last week,

18
00:03:48,495 --> 00:03:50,615
I've decided to go with
another investigator.

19
00:03:50,664 --> 00:03:51,664
Sorry.

20
00:03:53,734 --> 00:03:55,500
Hi, my name is Brad Loomis.

21
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:58,169
I'm with the investment firm
of James, Ashford and Town.

22
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:00,238
I'd like to talk to
you about invest...

23
00:04:15,689 --> 00:04:17,455
Sorry I'm late.

24
00:04:17,524 --> 00:04:18,668
Well, talk fast.

25
00:04:18,692 --> 00:04:20,892
My kids have got swim
lessons in half an hour.

26
00:04:21,995 --> 00:04:22,995
You heard her.

27
00:04:23,029 --> 00:04:24,963
Talk fast.

28
00:04:25,031 --> 00:04:28,345
Well, you... This
meeting wasn't my idea.

29
00:04:28,369 --> 00:04:30,301
But your secretary
called my secretary.

30
00:04:30,371 --> 00:04:31,881
Not mine.

31
00:04:31,905 --> 00:04:32,915
You called.

32
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,539
No, he called and told my son

33
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,419
I was supposed meet
you two here. I did not.

34
00:04:36,443 --> 00:04:37,876
What, you calling my son a liar?

35
00:04:37,945 --> 00:04:38,955
Wait a minute. Hold it.

36
00:04:38,979 --> 00:04:39,989
Hold it. Hold it.

37
00:04:40,013 --> 00:04:41,691
What the hell's going on here?

38
00:04:41,715 --> 00:04:43,982
Oh, my grandmother was right.

39
00:04:44,051 --> 00:04:46,317
She always said you can tell

40
00:04:46,386 --> 00:04:48,319
how well people know each other

41
00:04:48,388 --> 00:04:50,188
by how intensely they argue.

42
00:04:51,391 --> 00:04:53,992
Uh, Mr-Mr-Mr. Sands.

43
00:04:54,061 --> 00:04:57,495
Oh, and Mr. Barr, then,
and, uh, Mrs. Proctor.

44
00:04:57,564 --> 00:04:58,830
Uh, Ben Matlock.

45
00:04:58,899 --> 00:05:00,043
I'm sorry for the confusion.

46
00:05:00,067 --> 00:05:01,566
I called the meeting.

47
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:02,845
Would you care for a drink?

48
00:05:02,869 --> 00:05:04,335
What do you want?

49
00:05:04,404 --> 00:05:06,749
Uh, I'm just trying to find out

50
00:05:06,773 --> 00:05:08,651
who killed Rob
Casey. You remember

51
00:05:08,675 --> 00:05:09,607
Rob Casey.

52
00:05:09,676 --> 00:05:10,775
Uh, he was the man

53
00:05:10,844 --> 00:05:13,645
who was gonna
send each of you a set

54
00:05:13,713 --> 00:05:15,313
of these.

55
00:05:15,382 --> 00:05:16,525
Why would

56
00:05:16,549 --> 00:05:18,816
a complete stranger
send me a photograph?

57
00:05:18,885 --> 00:05:21,152
Well, he needed $40,000.

58
00:05:21,221 --> 00:05:23,321
And he needed it quick.

59
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:25,323
And, uh, my guess is that, uh,

60
00:05:25,392 --> 00:05:27,158
these, uh, pictures tell a story

61
00:05:27,227 --> 00:05:29,293
you'd assume
the police not hear.

62
00:05:29,363 --> 00:05:30,528
Are you saying

63
00:05:30,597 --> 00:05:33,064
he was trying to
blackmail one of us?

64
00:05:33,133 --> 00:05:34,632
Or-or all of you.

65
00:05:34,701 --> 00:05:36,679
But, as I say,
that's-that's a guess.

66
00:05:36,703 --> 00:05:38,447
The man with all
the answers is dead.

67
00:05:38,471 --> 00:05:42,006
Uh... is there anything
else, Mr. Matlock?

68
00:05:42,075 --> 00:05:43,508
Uh, as a matter of fact, yes.

69
00:05:43,577 --> 00:05:46,778
Uh... party favors.

70
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:48,780
There you are.

71
00:05:48,849 --> 00:05:50,782
Here you go.

72
00:06:09,002 --> 00:06:11,936
Hi.

73
00:06:12,005 --> 00:06:14,639
I'd like to see Jeffrey Barr.

74
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:17,909
He had some kind of
emergency meeting.

75
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:24,382
Are you interested in having
something videotaped?

76
00:06:24,450 --> 00:06:25,550
Uh, no.

77
00:06:25,619 --> 00:06:26,718
It's personal.

78
00:06:26,786 --> 00:06:27,952
I'm an old friend of his.

79
00:06:28,021 --> 00:06:29,721
Tyler Hudson.

80
00:06:29,789 --> 00:06:31,909
You have heard him
speak of me, haven't you?

81
00:06:32,825 --> 00:06:34,892
No.

82
00:06:34,961 --> 00:06:37,895
Well, I don't get
into town very often.

83
00:06:37,964 --> 00:06:42,534
I guess out of
sight, out of mind.

84
00:06:44,638 --> 00:06:46,571
Do you mind if I wait?

85
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:48,072
Sure.

86
00:06:48,141 --> 00:06:51,576
You can wait in my office.

87
00:06:51,645 --> 00:06:54,980
Uh... out here is okay.

88
00:06:57,617 --> 00:06:59,550
Excuse me.

89
00:07:05,125 --> 00:07:08,059
Hello, Vid-Proof.

90
00:07:09,629 --> 00:07:10,896
Oh, that's terrible.

91
00:07:10,964 --> 00:07:12,330
I'm so sorry.

92
00:07:12,398 --> 00:07:13,331
Hold on.

93
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:15,333
I'll pull your tape right now.

94
00:07:28,515 --> 00:07:30,448
Mm-hmm.

95
00:07:53,707 --> 00:07:56,908
I have your tape right
here, Mr. Franklin.

96
00:07:56,977 --> 00:07:59,577
Shall I messenger it over
to your insurance company?

97
00:07:59,646 --> 00:08:00,845
That's what we're here for.

98
00:08:00,914 --> 00:08:04,282
If you need anything
else, just call us.

99
00:08:20,967 --> 00:08:22,900
Mr. Hudson?

100
00:08:50,396 --> 00:08:52,329
Hello, Linda.

101
00:08:54,333 --> 00:08:55,867
How'd you get in here?

102
00:08:55,936 --> 00:08:58,637
Tyler.

103
00:08:58,705 --> 00:09:01,806
He's the reason your
answering machine doesn't work.

104
00:09:01,875 --> 00:09:04,843
We figured you'd
stop by to see why.

105
00:09:04,912 --> 00:09:06,344
Please just leave.

106
00:09:06,413 --> 00:09:09,548
Somebody doesn't
want you to talk to me.

107
00:09:09,616 --> 00:09:11,683
You don't understand.

108
00:09:12,785 --> 00:09:14,885
Then make me understand.

109
00:09:15,989 --> 00:09:18,924
They got my boy.

110
00:09:18,992 --> 00:09:21,426
Someone broke in here last week

111
00:09:21,494 --> 00:09:23,995
and they stole the log
I kept on Rob Casey.

112
00:09:24,064 --> 00:09:25,530
And left a note.

113
00:09:25,598 --> 00:09:27,176
Said they have David.

114
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:30,134
If I didn't testify
against Michael Koskoff

115
00:09:30,203 --> 00:09:31,770
I'd never see him again.

116
00:09:31,838 --> 00:09:33,772
I'm sorry.

117
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:35,485
I'm just trying to
buy some time.

118
00:09:35,509 --> 00:09:37,442
I'm going crazy.

119
00:09:37,511 --> 00:09:41,479
Did they say when
they'd contact you again?

120
00:09:41,548 --> 00:09:43,481
Sometime today.

121
00:09:43,549 --> 00:09:46,317
David has asthma.

122
00:09:46,386 --> 00:09:48,887
If he gets upset or frightened,
he's gonna get very sick.

123
00:09:48,955 --> 00:09:51,222
Does he know his medication?

124
00:09:51,290 --> 00:09:54,258
He knows what he needs.

125
00:09:54,327 --> 00:09:56,260
Well, he's-he's bright.

126
00:09:56,329 --> 00:09:58,029
And, uh, he's inventive.

127
00:09:58,098 --> 00:10:00,076
Maybe he'll figure
out a way to get it.

128
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:03,267
If whoever has him lets him.

129
00:10:03,336 --> 00:10:05,536
And why would they care?

130
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:10,508
Somebody in on this thing
made a desperate move.

131
00:10:10,577 --> 00:10:12,510
Very desperate.

132
00:10:27,326 --> 00:10:29,639
Somebody's coming
to this drugstore

133
00:10:29,663 --> 00:10:31,140
to pick up David's medicine.

134
00:10:31,164 --> 00:10:33,175
He's probably in there already.

135
00:10:33,199 --> 00:10:34,632
So soon?

136
00:10:34,701 --> 00:10:37,513
Mr. Marshal said someone
called in the prescription.

137
00:10:37,537 --> 00:10:39,203
Well, that was less
than an hour ago.

138
00:10:39,272 --> 00:10:43,141
Linda, when this guy comes
out of the drugstore, be cool.

139
00:10:43,209 --> 00:10:44,853
Sure. The object here

140
00:10:44,877 --> 00:10:47,856
is for him to lead us
to David, okay? Okay.

141
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,814
All right.

142
00:10:51,884 --> 00:10:54,763
Now, look, Linda,
just take it easy, okay?

143
00:10:54,787 --> 00:10:55,931
This is going to work.

144
00:10:55,955 --> 00:10:57,888
I promise.

145
00:11:03,963 --> 00:11:05,897
Hello?

146
00:11:05,965 --> 00:11:07,899
Thank you, Mr. Marshal.

147
00:11:11,270 --> 00:11:13,838
There you go.

148
00:11:13,907 --> 00:11:15,050
Yeah, that's him.

149
00:11:15,074 --> 00:11:16,952
That's one of Dominic
Vincent's hoods.

150
00:11:16,976 --> 00:11:19,344
Linda! Linda!

151
00:11:22,582 --> 00:11:24,542
Where is my kid?!

152
00:11:32,192 --> 00:11:33,591
Get him!

153
00:11:33,659 --> 00:11:35,539
Tyler, get him!

154
00:11:43,569 --> 00:11:45,603
Get him!

155
00:11:53,413 --> 00:11:55,346
♪ ♪

156
00:12:23,510 --> 00:12:25,388
Here's the kid's prescription.

157
00:12:25,412 --> 00:12:28,346
I had some
trouble picking it up.

158
00:12:38,991 --> 00:12:40,169
<i>Ben Matlock.</i>

159
00:12:40,193 --> 00:12:41,337
<i>Hello, Ben?</i>

160
00:12:41,361 --> 00:12:42,760
Tyler, where are you?

161
00:12:42,829 --> 00:12:45,341
I'm across the street
from a house at 6624

162
00:12:45,365 --> 00:12:47,098
Langdon Avenue.

163
00:12:47,167 --> 00:12:49,000
I saw him.

164
00:12:49,068 --> 00:12:50,712
Uh, one of Dominic
Vincent's goons

165
00:12:50,736 --> 00:12:52,648
just dropped off
his prescription.

166
00:12:52,672 --> 00:12:54,172
Yeah, well, we can't do anything

167
00:12:54,241 --> 00:12:57,041
that might get David hurt,
so just don't do anything.

168
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:59,376
Stay in your car,
watch the house.

169
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:00,377
You got it.

170
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:01,478
Right.

171
00:13:01,547 --> 00:13:04,648
We have to do something.

172
00:13:04,717 --> 00:13:06,817
I know.

173
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:19,374
Mr. Matlock, I'm shocked.

174
00:13:19,398 --> 00:13:20,764
I respect family.

175
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:22,333
I wouldn't kidnap a kid.

176
00:13:22,402 --> 00:13:25,403
Whoever took David
Hansfield works for you.

177
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:27,583
Hey, Dom?

178
00:13:27,607 --> 00:13:29,307
You birdied the sucker.

179
00:13:29,375 --> 00:13:30,942
All right.

180
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:32,988
I don't know anything
about this kidnapping,

181
00:13:33,012 --> 00:13:35,380
but I'll look into it.

182
00:13:35,448 --> 00:13:36,848
I appreciate it.

183
00:13:36,917 --> 00:13:39,684
I expect to see David very soon.

184
00:13:39,752 --> 00:13:41,552
With a little luck, Mr. Matlock.

185
00:13:41,621 --> 00:13:44,522
You do believe
in luck, don't you?

186
00:13:44,591 --> 00:13:47,825
Whatever works, Mr. Vincent.

187
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:07,790
Linda, what the hell
are you doing here?

188
00:14:07,814 --> 00:14:09,558
You didn't think I was
gonna wait in the office?

189
00:14:09,582 --> 00:14:10,726
I guess not.

190
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:11,850
How many men in there?

191
00:14:11,918 --> 00:14:13,251
There's one, I think.

192
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:14,864
The guy that grabbed David left.

193
00:14:14,888 --> 00:14:16,165
Let's go. Wait a minute.

194
00:14:16,189 --> 00:14:18,166
Now, Ben specifically
said for us to wait.

195
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,658
Let go of me. Wait a minute!

196
00:14:20,727 --> 00:14:21,804
Now, what are you gonna do,

197
00:14:21,828 --> 00:14:23,238
just walk up and
knock on the door?

198
00:14:23,262 --> 00:14:24,095
That's my kid in there!

199
00:14:24,163 --> 00:14:25,263
You got a better idea?

200
00:14:25,331 --> 00:14:26,475
Hold on a minute.

201
00:14:26,499 --> 00:14:28,566
Close the door!

202
00:14:28,634 --> 00:14:31,469
If you're not careful, you
might wind up getting him hurt.

203
00:14:31,538 --> 00:14:34,672
Let's be smart about this, okay?

204
00:14:36,242 --> 00:14:38,175
Stop or I'll shoot!

205
00:14:40,246 --> 00:14:42,947
Here's pop and chips, kid.

206
00:14:43,016 --> 00:14:44,415
Knock yourself out.

207
00:14:46,686 --> 00:14:48,326
Oh, no!

208
00:14:48,355 --> 00:14:49,988
There they go again.

209
00:14:51,591 --> 00:14:55,093
And this time, I'm
going to stop him.

210
00:14:55,161 --> 00:14:59,964
Hi. Do you know
anything about cars?

211
00:15:00,032 --> 00:15:02,112
I think there's something
wrong with mine.

212
00:15:04,504 --> 00:15:06,436
I don't know.

213
00:15:06,506 --> 00:15:08,872
Please do something.

214
00:15:15,548 --> 00:15:17,326
I don't know if I
can do anything.

215
00:15:17,350 --> 00:15:19,910
Bless you.

216
00:15:26,993 --> 00:15:28,926
Yeah, this is... See?

217
00:15:34,467 --> 00:15:35,999
Your radiator's bone dry.

218
00:15:36,068 --> 00:15:37,880
When's the last
time you checked it?

219
00:15:37,904 --> 00:15:39,837
I don't know.

220
00:15:39,906 --> 00:15:41,005
Never.

221
00:15:42,375 --> 00:15:44,455
It'll be here any minute.

222
00:15:51,250 --> 00:15:52,516
Hello, David.

223
00:15:52,585 --> 00:15:53,818
Remember me?

224
00:15:53,886 --> 00:15:56,231
You're that guy who
works for my mom.

225
00:15:56,255 --> 00:15:57,788
<i>With</i> your mom.

226
00:15:57,857 --> 00:15:59,791
I work<i> with</i> your mother.

227
00:15:59,859 --> 00:16:01,269
Where is she? She's outside.

228
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:02,993
I want her to come in.

229
00:16:03,062 --> 00:16:05,329
She wants you to come out.

230
00:16:05,398 --> 00:16:06,797
No!

231
00:16:06,866 --> 00:16:07,965
Hmm.

232
00:16:08,034 --> 00:16:10,201
David, your mother
is waiting for you

233
00:16:10,269 --> 00:16:11,569
outside.

234
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:13,705
That's what the other guy said.

235
00:16:13,773 --> 00:16:14,773
No!

236
00:16:16,508 --> 00:16:17,975
Hmm.

237
00:16:18,044 --> 00:16:19,254
<i>Did you have</i>

238
00:16:19,278 --> 00:16:21,311
a hose or-or a bucket? A what?!

239
00:16:21,381 --> 00:16:23,247
A bucket. A bucket.

240
00:16:23,316 --> 00:16:26,050
No. Maybe some,
uh, distilled water?

241
00:16:26,119 --> 00:16:27,985
It-It comes in a bottle.

242
00:16:28,054 --> 00:16:29,231
All right, I'll get
some of that.

243
00:16:29,255 --> 00:16:31,355
That'd be great. You mean now?

244
00:16:31,424 --> 00:16:33,702
Well, yeah, I mean now.
What...? What was...?

245
00:16:33,726 --> 00:16:35,170
There's this thing. I
think... I think this is it.

246
00:16:35,194 --> 00:16:36,672
Thing... You... What? What?

247
00:16:39,065 --> 00:16:41,031
That's the kid's mother!

248
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:43,100
Oh!

249
00:16:43,169 --> 00:16:44,480
Oh.

250
00:16:46,105 --> 00:16:48,305
Hey, lady, get
back in the house!

251
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,124
Ow, lady! No!

252
00:16:55,148 --> 00:16:56,292
Oh!

253
00:17:08,494 --> 00:17:11,862
Hey... Move in...

254
00:17:24,811 --> 00:17:27,371
Hey.

255
00:17:30,850 --> 00:17:32,027
Oh. There you go.

256
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:33,595
Say, he's all right. Oh, David.

257
00:17:33,619 --> 00:17:35,319
He's okay.

258
00:17:35,388 --> 00:17:37,948
Let's see...

259
00:17:48,201 --> 00:17:50,134
<i>Thank you.</i>

260
00:17:52,238 --> 00:17:54,483
Vincent's hood died before
he reached the hospital.

261
00:17:54,507 --> 00:17:57,241
Oh, what about the one
who was holding David?

262
00:17:57,310 --> 00:17:59,076
He was one of the lesser hoods.

263
00:17:59,144 --> 00:18:01,657
Oh, he just hadn't been
convicted of murder yet.

264
00:18:04,684 --> 00:18:08,218
I had a feeling you'd
go after David yourself.

265
00:18:08,287 --> 00:18:12,668
I couldn't help it. I... I know.

266
00:18:12,692 --> 00:18:14,625
He's your son.

267
00:18:15,894 --> 00:18:18,996
I'm glad I have a
hot line to the police.

268
00:18:19,065 --> 00:18:21,631
Thanks.

269
00:18:21,701 --> 00:18:22,933
Mm.

270
00:18:23,002 --> 00:18:26,103
I've caused you
a lot of trouble.

271
00:18:26,172 --> 00:18:28,972
I lied in court,
I hurt the case.

272
00:18:29,042 --> 00:18:30,941
Remember I told you,

273
00:18:31,010 --> 00:18:33,210
being a woman in
this business isn't easy.

274
