00:36:09,233 --> 00:36:11,634
Their presence in there
would distract the students.

539
00:36:11,703 --> 00:36:13,503
Hmm.

540
00:36:13,571 --> 00:36:16,706
Shoulders back, wrists down.

541
00:36:16,775 --> 00:36:18,942
Tempo, tempo.

542
00:36:22,848 --> 00:36:24,781
Uh, do you always
keep these doors closed?

543
00:36:24,850 --> 00:36:25,782
Yes.

544
00:36:25,851 --> 00:36:28,451
So you wouldn't know for sure

545
00:36:28,520 --> 00:36:30,986
whether she stayed or left.

546
00:36:31,055 --> 00:36:34,324
No, I wouldn't.

547
00:36:34,392 --> 00:36:36,826
Mrs. Proctor will be
here at 4:00 tomorrow

548
00:36:36,894 --> 00:36:38,494
for Artie's regular lesson.

549
00:36:38,563 --> 00:36:40,308
Shall I ask her
and then call you?

550
00:36:40,332 --> 00:36:42,866
No, no, no, please
don't say anything.

551
00:36:42,935 --> 00:36:44,334
All right.

552
00:36:44,403 --> 00:36:46,502
Thank you for your time, though.

553
00:36:47,606 --> 00:36:49,706
Uh, y-you say, uh,

554
00:36:49,775 --> 00:36:53,976
Artie-Artie's regular lesson
was Wednesdays at 4:00?

555
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:57,492
Yes. But on the... BOTH: 17th...

556
00:36:57,516 --> 00:36:58,915
he came at 6:00?

557
00:36:58,983 --> 00:37:01,284
Oh, Mrs. Proctor
called the night before

558
00:37:01,353 --> 00:37:03,319
and asked if she
could reschedule.

559
00:37:03,388 --> 00:37:06,256
Artie's one of my
favorites; I said fine.

560
00:37:06,325 --> 00:37:08,090
Oh, well, that's fine.

561
00:37:08,159 --> 00:37:09,804
Thank you. Uh-huh.

562
00:37:09,828 --> 00:37:11,528
We enjoyed that.

563
00:37:19,203 --> 00:37:22,438
Casey's house is
five minutes from here.

564
00:37:22,507 --> 00:37:23,906
She killed him.

565
00:37:23,975 --> 00:37:27,010
She snuck out, she killed
him, she snuck back in.

566
00:37:34,853 --> 00:37:36,853
Oh, he wants my spot.

567
00:37:57,075 --> 00:37:59,053
<i>The note said
if I didn't testify</i>

568
00:37:59,077 --> 00:38:00,421
against Michael Koskoff,

569
00:38:00,445 --> 00:38:01,856
that I'd never see my son again.

570
00:38:01,880 --> 00:38:03,245
Huh.

571
00:38:03,314 --> 00:38:04,480
So is that what you did?

572
00:38:06,585 --> 00:38:09,452
I testified earlier that I saw

573
00:38:09,520 --> 00:38:13,255
Michael Koskoff leaving
the scene of the murder

574
00:38:13,324 --> 00:38:15,825
when, in fact, I didn't
see anybody at all.

575
00:38:15,894 --> 00:38:20,829
Why would someone force
you to lie in court like that?

576
00:38:20,898 --> 00:38:23,732
So that Michael Koskoff
would be convicted and...

577
00:38:23,801 --> 00:38:27,070
the real murderer... the
person who kidnapped my son,

578
00:38:27,138 --> 00:38:30,706
would get away.

579
00:38:30,775 --> 00:38:33,809
When you found your son,
he was wearing a jacket.

580
00:38:33,878 --> 00:38:35,123
Yes.

581
00:38:35,147 --> 00:38:38,481
I asked you to bring that
jacket to court with you today.

582
00:38:38,550 --> 00:38:40,483
This is it.

583
00:38:40,552 --> 00:38:43,053
I ask that this jacket be marked

584
00:38:43,121 --> 00:38:45,655
Defense Exhibit
"J" for identification.

585
00:38:45,723 --> 00:38:47,022
It shall be so marked.

586
00:38:47,092 --> 00:38:48,092
Thank you.

587
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:50,126
Uh, is this your son's jacket?

588
00:38:50,195 --> 00:38:52,128
No.

589
00:38:52,197 --> 00:38:55,798
And when I examined it...

590
00:38:55,867 --> 00:38:57,611
I found this label
sewn into the lining.

591
00:38:57,635 --> 00:38:59,802
What does it say?

592
00:38:59,871 --> 00:39:03,139
It says "Artie Proctor."

593
00:39:03,207 --> 00:39:07,176
Nancy Proctor, Mr. Barr
and Mr. Sands' mutual friend,

594
00:39:07,244 --> 00:39:09,846
has a son named
Artie, doesn't she?

595
00:39:09,914 --> 00:39:12,115
Yes, she does.

596
00:39:13,684 --> 00:39:16,619
No further questions.

597
00:39:16,688 --> 00:39:18,988
No questions.

598
00:39:19,057 --> 00:39:20,756
Witness may step down.

599
00:39:20,825 --> 00:39:22,559
Mr. Matlock.

600
00:39:22,627 --> 00:39:26,095
Call Nancy Proctor to the stand.

601
00:39:26,164 --> 00:39:29,665
You recognize this coat?

602
00:39:29,734 --> 00:39:31,501
Yes, it used to be my son's.

603
00:39:31,569 --> 00:39:33,068
Used to be?

604
00:39:33,138 --> 00:39:34,637
He lost it several weeks ago.

605
00:39:34,705 --> 00:39:37,940
I have no idea how
it ended up here.

606
00:39:38,009 --> 00:39:42,212
I think you have
a very good idea.

607
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:44,814
I think you're a good mother
and you would never let

608
00:39:44,882 --> 00:39:49,586
anybody's little boy go
without a warm jacket.

609
00:39:49,654 --> 00:39:52,555
Are you saying that I
had something to do

610
00:39:52,624 --> 00:39:53,664
with the kidnapping?

611
00:39:53,691 --> 00:39:56,926
You had everything
to do with it.

612
00:39:56,995 --> 00:40:00,529
That is not true.

613
00:40:00,598 --> 00:40:03,599
I have two small
children of my own.

614
00:40:03,668 --> 00:40:06,569
I think kidnapping is
the most despicable,

615
00:40:06,637 --> 00:40:08,571
the most heinous of all crimes.

616
00:40:10,675 --> 00:40:13,276
And that's exactly
why you thought

617
00:40:13,345 --> 00:40:15,078
you could get away with it.

618
00:40:15,146 --> 00:40:18,147
You knew you had a surefire
way to get another mother...

619
00:40:18,216 --> 00:40:19,148
Linda Hansfield...

620
00:40:19,217 --> 00:40:22,785
To help convict Michael Koskoff

621
00:40:22,854 --> 00:40:25,488
and get you off the hook
for the murder of Rob Casey.

622
00:40:25,557 --> 00:40:26,489
Objection.

623
00:40:26,558 --> 00:40:27,668
No foundation.

624
00:40:27,692 --> 00:40:30,426
Assumes facts not in evidence.

625
00:40:30,495 --> 00:40:31,672
Sustained.

626
00:40:31,696 --> 00:40:33,162
Okay.

627
00:40:33,231 --> 00:40:37,766
Um, uh, where were you
between 6:00 and 6:30 p.m.

628
00:40:37,836 --> 00:40:39,936
on March 17?

629
00:40:40,004 --> 00:40:41,971
I was at my son's
weekly piano lesson.

630
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:43,572
I was waiting for him there.

631
00:40:43,641 --> 00:40:47,010
Uh, does he usually
have his lesson at 6:00?

632
00:40:47,078 --> 00:40:48,745
Well, usually it's at 4:00.

633
00:40:48,813 --> 00:40:50,212
I, uh, had to reschedule it.

634
00:40:50,282 --> 00:40:51,481
I forget why.

635
00:40:51,549 --> 00:40:53,994
But you were waiting for
him right there in the room?

636
00:40:54,018 --> 00:40:55,050
Yes.

637
00:40:55,119 --> 00:40:56,619
Now, are you sure?

638
00:40:56,688 --> 00:40:59,855
We have spoken
with the music teacher.

639
00:40:59,924 --> 00:41:01,364
Well, I was actually
in another room.

640
00:41:01,393 --> 00:41:02,525
Uh-huh.

641
00:41:02,594 --> 00:41:06,296
Uh, where, where did
you park that evening?

642
00:41:06,364 --> 00:41:08,364
Where did I park?

643
00:41:08,433 --> 00:41:09,443
Objection.

644
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:10,467
Relevance?

645
00:41:10,501 --> 00:41:12,235
Your Honor, I must be able

646
00:41:12,303 --> 00:41:14,002
to ask this witness
where she parked.

647
00:41:14,071 --> 00:41:17,239
It goes to the alibi, and
this coat demands it.

648
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:19,508
Overruled.

649
00:41:19,578 --> 00:41:22,278
So, so... thank you... Where
did you park that evening?

650
00:41:22,346 --> 00:41:24,291
Which side of the
street... North or south?

651
00:41:24,315 --> 00:41:27,583
The... south side.

652
00:41:27,652 --> 00:41:29,285
Mm! Mm, mm, mm.

653
00:41:29,354 --> 00:41:31,053
Did you get a ticket?

654
00:41:31,122 --> 00:41:32,489
No.

655
00:41:32,557 --> 00:41:33,823
No?

656
00:41:33,892 --> 00:41:38,795
Well, uh, these
people all parked

657
00:41:38,863 --> 00:41:43,533
on the same side of the
street that you say you parked,

658
00:41:43,601 --> 00:41:44,612
but they all got tickets.

659
00:41:44,636 --> 00:41:46,969
Do you know why?

660
00:41:47,038 --> 00:41:48,671
I have no idea.

661
00:41:48,740 --> 00:41:50,406
Rush hour traffic regulation.

662
00:41:50,474 --> 00:41:53,642
There's a sign right
in front of the house.

663
00:41:53,711 --> 00:41:57,346
Maybe because you usually
go at 4:00, you never noticed it.

664
00:41:57,415 --> 00:42:00,482
Now, why did all these
people get parking tickets

665
00:42:00,551 --> 00:42:01,850
and you didn't?

666
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:03,798
The meter maid
somehow missed me.

667
00:42:05,022 --> 00:42:08,424
Or maybe you missed her.

668
00:42:08,493 --> 00:42:10,459
Did you sneak out of that house,

669
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:13,962
drive the less than two
miles to Rob Casey's house,

670
00:42:14,031 --> 00:42:15,464
go in, kill him,

671
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:18,768
drive back, sneak
back in the library

672
00:42:18,836 --> 00:42:21,704
at the music teacher's just
before the lesson ended?

673
00:42:21,773 --> 00:42:22,838
No.

674
00:42:22,907 --> 00:42:25,018
You were in on that
jewelry store heist

675
00:42:25,042 --> 00:42:27,677
four years ago, weren't you?

676
00:42:27,745 --> 00:42:30,079
And everything
went fine for a while,

677
00:42:30,147 --> 00:42:34,717
but then Rob Casey
began to realize

678
00:42:34,786 --> 00:42:38,153
the only way out of his problems

679
00:42:38,223 --> 00:42:40,656
was to blackmail you,

680
00:42:40,725 --> 00:42:43,426
and you knew that he
worked for Michael Koskoff

681
00:42:43,494 --> 00:42:45,105
and you knew where
the gun was kept

682
00:42:45,129 --> 00:42:48,631
and you stole that gun
and you killed Rob Casey.

683
00:42:48,700 --> 00:42:53,069
None of that is true.

684
00:42:53,138 --> 00:42:55,704
Where'd you go after
the music lesson?

685
00:42:55,773 --> 00:42:57,507
I, uh, I took my son

686
00:42:57,576 --> 00:42:59,875
to get ice cream,
as I always do.

687
00:42:59,944 --> 00:43:01,055
Uh-huh.

688
00:43:01,079 --> 00:43:03,513
You went to a parlor
at Ninth and Maple?

689
00:43:03,581 --> 00:43:04,914
Yes.

690
00:43:04,982 --> 00:43:09,485
And you ordered one butter pecan
cone and one fudge ripple cone?

691
00:43:09,554 --> 00:43:10,686
Yes.

692
00:43:10,755 --> 00:43:15,057
And you paid $1.80 for
them in exact change?

693
00:43:15,126 --> 00:43:16,559
I don't remember.

694
00:43:17,795 --> 00:43:22,331
Well, the boy who waited
on you remembered...

695
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:24,867
because...

696
00:43:24,935 --> 00:43:28,537
this is one of the coins
you paid him with...

697
00:43:28,606 --> 00:43:31,440
A 1936 quarter.

698
00:43:31,509 --> 00:43:34,477
He kept it because
he knew it was old.

699
00:43:34,545 --> 00:43:38,314
He thought maybe it
was valuable, and it was

700
00:43:38,383 --> 00:43:41,484
much more valuable
than he thought.

701
00:43:41,552 --> 00:43:43,319
It's a proof.

702
00:43:43,388 --> 00:43:45,721
Thing about a coin like this is

703
00:43:45,790 --> 00:43:47,923
the only place you
can find them now is

704
00:43:47,993 --> 00:43:51,227
in a collection or in a, a store

705
00:43:51,296 --> 00:43:54,830
like Rob Casey worked in.

706
00:43:54,899 --> 00:43:56,832
What were you doing with it?

707
00:43:57,936 --> 00:44:00,403
I have no idea.

708
00:44:00,471 --> 00:44:05,441
Thing about coin proofs
is you have to have

709
00:44:05,510 --> 00:44:09,746
a whole set from
one year... Penny,

710
00:44:09,814 --> 00:44:13,149
nickel, dime, quarter,
50-cent piece...

711
00:44:13,218 --> 00:44:14,884
And Rob Casey had that.

712
00:44:14,952 --> 00:44:19,588
Kept it in a plastic
box on a table.

713
00:44:19,657 --> 00:44:22,558
I know because I found it.

714
00:44:22,627 --> 00:44:26,628
It was melted, but
everything was there

715
00:44:26,697 --> 00:44:29,143
except this quarter.

716
00:44:29,167 --> 00:44:31,000
I found, I found a quarter.

717
00:44:31,069 --> 00:44:34,303
It was a 1987.

718
00:44:34,372 --> 00:44:40,876
Now, how do you suppose
that 1987 quarter was there,

719
00:44:40,945 --> 00:44:44,347
and you wound up with this 1936?

720
00:44:44,416 --> 00:44:47,950
I don't know.

721
00:44:48,018 --> 00:44:51,020
How about this?

722
00:44:51,088 --> 00:44:54,990
You went over there ostensibly
to give him the blackmail money.

723
00:44:55,059 --> 00:44:57,894
He knew you, so he
let you in the back door.

724
00:44:57,962 --> 00:44:59,673
You put your purse
down on the table

725
00:44:59,697 --> 00:45:02,732
where he kept
his coin collection,

726
00:45:02,801 --> 00:45:06,669
opened your purse to take
out the blackmail money,

727
00:45:06,738 --> 00:45:08,516
but you took out a pistol.

728
00:45:08,540 --> 00:45:09,906
I don't know what happened then.

729
00:45:09,974 --> 00:45:11,819
You shot him and
he fell on the table

730
00:45:11,843 --> 00:45:14,076
or he jumped at
you as you shot him

731
00:45:14,145 --> 00:45:15,912
and you both fell on the table.

732
00:45:15,980 --> 00:45:20,716
Anyhow, you and him and
the table and your purse

733
00:45:20,785 --> 00:45:23,586
and a coin collection all
went to hell in a tea kettle.

734
00:45:23,655 --> 00:45:25,755
I mean, stuff went everywhere.

735
00:45:26,858 --> 00:45:28,068
Well, you had to
get out of there,

736
00:45:28,092 --> 00:45:29,292
so you picked up your purse,

737
00:45:29,360 --> 00:45:31,305
see if you had anything
else on the floor,

738
00:45:31,329 --> 00:45:34,163
maybe lipstick or powder
puff or a comb or something.

739
00:45:34,231 --> 00:45:37,433
Here's a coin, pick it up,
put it in there, get out of there.

740
00:45:39,504 --> 00:45:42,271
And then you went
to the ice cream parlor

741
00:45:42,339 --> 00:45:45,240
and bought some ice cream.

742
00:45:45,309 --> 00:45:52,014
Only thing is you overpaid
by almost a thousand dollars.

743
00:45:54,084 --> 00:45:58,086
He was blackmailing
all of you, wasn't he?

744
00:45:59,189 --> 00:46:04,560
How did you get
picked to kill him?

745
00:46:04,629 --> 00:46:10,566
Did, did you volunteer
or did you draw straws?

746
00:46:18,309 --> 00:46:21,444
Maybe you ought
to invoke the Fifth.

747
00:46:27,785 --> 00:46:29,763
How do you feel?

748
00:46:29,787 --> 00:46:32,622
Happy is how I feel,
happy and, and relieved

749
00:46:32,690 --> 00:46:35,390
and eager to get
back to my coin shop.

750
00:46:38,529 --> 00:46:42,865
Tyler.

751
00:46:42,934 --> 00:46:44,566
Congratulations.

752
00:46:44,635 --> 00:46:46,202
Congratulations to you.

753
00:46:46,270 --> 00:46:48,871
You know, we make
a pretty good team.

754
00:46:48,940 --> 00:46:51,707
This is going to work out okay.

755
00:46:51,776 --> 00:46:54,243
Uh,<i> what</i> is going
to work out okay?

756
00:46:54,311 --> 00:46:56,623
Well, I'm glad to see you've
settled your differences.

757
00:46:56,647 --> 00:46:58,192
This is going to work out okay.

758
00:46:58,216 --> 00:47:00,182
What's going to work out okay?

759
00:47:00,251 --> 00:47:03,252
Linda's agreed to work
with us from time to time.

760
00:47:03,321 --> 00:47:04,486
Do you like hot dogs?

761
00:47:04,555 --> 00:47:06,388
Uh, can't stand 'em.

762
00:47:06,457 --> 00:47:08,490
This is not going
to work out okay.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
